# Security boundary

Source of truth: `docs/security.md`, `docs/architecture.md` (Authentication), ADR-0002.

## MUST NOT

- Query Supabase directly from this service
- Store or ship Supabase credentials in this service
- Accept or forward a user JWT so this service can access Supabase/RLS
- Implement farm ownership or user authorization rules here

## MUST

- Treat financial calculations as operating on an **explicit, scoped financial input contract**
- Keep **service-to-service authentication** distinct from **user authentication** (user auth stays at the App Platform)

## Target vs current

Service-to-service auth is the **documented trust model**. It may not be implemented on the API yet. When adding authentication, follow `docs/security.md` and ADR-0002 — do not “temporarily” use user JWTs for data access. Do not implement a full auth stack unless the task explicitly requests it.

## On risky requests

If a task appears to require direct database access, JWT forwarding for data access, or a new trust relationship: treat it as an architectural/security decision. Stop, cite `docs/security.md`, and do not implement it as a local convenience.
